[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735695696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2735695696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2735695696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jD2dQ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T08:20:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T08:22:30Z","body":"Please provide actual steps to reproduce, or ideally a reproduction project.\nThere's a lot left to guessing here: how is the CSG shape set up? Which shape type? How are you calling `intersect_shape`?\n\nThe issue doesn't mention Jolt at all but based on your comment in #104310 I assume this is only reproducible with Jolt selected as the 3D physics engine? Since it's not the default it needs to be made clear in a bug report.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735695696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735920213","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2735920213","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2735920213,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jEtRV","user":{"login":"eddieataberk","id":48696693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4Njk2Njkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48696693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk","html_url":"https://github.com/eddieataberk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T09:36:18Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T09:36:18Z","body":"Yes it is Jolt also it seems the issue only happens if the origin of the params.transform is inside of the CSG shape.  You can attatch following code to a Node3D and click test query button.\n\n```\n\n@tool\nextends Node3D\n\n@export_tool_button('Test Query') var test_button := test_query\n\nfunc test_query() -> void:\n\tvar params := PhysicsShapeQueryParameters3D.new()\n\tparams.transform = global_transform\n\tparams.shape = BoxShape3D.new()\n\tvar result := get_world_3d().direct_space_state.intersect_shape(params)\n\tprint(result)\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2735920213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736881247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2736881247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2736881247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jIX5f","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T14:37:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T14:37:24Z","body":"@eddieataberk Just to clarify, are you seeing the same behavior if you switch to using Godot Physics as the 3D physics engine instead?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736881247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736992067","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2736992067","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2736992067,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jIy9D","user":{"login":"eddieataberk","id":48696693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4Njk2Njkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48696693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk","html_url":"https://github.com/eddieataberk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:07:00Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T15:07:00Z","body":"> [@eddieataberk](https://github.com/eddieataberk) Just to clarify, are you seeing the same behavior if you switch to using Godot Physics as the 3D physics engine instead?\n\nyes i do actually i tested it with a commit before this one godot phyiscs doesn't detect the shape on that too while jolt physics detecting the shape.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736992067/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737071436","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2737071436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2737071436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jJGVM","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:28:36Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T15:29:09Z","body":"Right, then this is not really a regression, nor even a bug, technically speaking.\n\nThe behavior you were relying on prior to #104310 was the bug, where `backface_collision` was always enabled for any `ConcavePolygonShape3D`, which is the physics shape that CSG uses \"under the hood\".\n\nUnfortunately the CSG nodes don't offer any way to enable this `backface_collision` property for its underlying `ConcavePolygonShape3D`, which you would need to do in this case, so the only real workaround would be to do the following:\n\n1. Child your CSG node to a new `StaticBody3D`.\n2. Disable the `use_collision` property for your CSG node.\n3. Select your CSG node.\n4. Click the \"CSG\" button in the viewport toolbar.\n5. Click \"Bake Collision Shape\".\n6. Select the newly created `*BakedCollisionShape3D` node.\n7. Expand its inner `shape` property/resource.\n8. Enable the `backface_collision` property on it.\n\nYou would unfortunately need to do this every time you changed the CSG parameters, so might not be a great solution, but it's the only one there is.\n\nThere's probably a good argument for just exposing `backface_collision` on the CSG shapes, so you don't have to jump through hoops like this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737071436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737109788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2737109788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2737109788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jJPsc","user":{"login":"eddieataberk","id":48696693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4Njk2Njkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48696693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk","html_url":"https://github.com/eddieataberk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddieataberk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:38:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T15:38:38Z","body":"Yeah. in this case exposing backface_collision seem the most reasonable. Is there a way to call Bake Collision Shape from gdscript?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737109788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737129702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104343#issuecomment-2737129702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104343","id":2737129702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jJUjm","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:43:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T15:43:45Z","body":"> Is there a way to call Bake Collision Shape from gdscript?\n\nYes, you can call the [`bake_collision_shape()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_csgshape3d.html#class-csgshape3d-method-bake-collision-shape) method on any `CSGShape3D`, which returns a `ConcavePolygonShape3D`. Note that this can be quite expensive though, depending on the complexity of the geometry, as mentioned in the documentation there.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737129702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]